     DEFECT FOUND. Details in F1.

Blocking finding F1 (defect, routes to Green):
- The S2 guards do not scan source files for disable comments, and the real
  tree hides live oxlint findings behind them. Strategy section 8 names the
  defense for the risk "Zero warnings by blanket disable": case 7, "no source
  file under apps/ or packages/ has `/* oxlint-disable` (block form). Each
  `oxlint-disable-next-line` has ` -- ` and a reason" (test-strategy.md:539).
  The plan S2 Test (Red) task (plan.md:286-297) holds cases 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9,
  and 9b only. No case scans the sources, and the strategy's proposed case 7
  would itself be vacuous, because the tree uses the `eslint-disable`
  spellings, not `oxlint-disable`.
- Facts at this HEAD: 49 tracked files under apps/ and packages/ hold a
  disable directive (7 blanket block disables, 53 eslint-disable-next-line,
  3 oxlint-disable-next-line, 1 eslint-disable-line; 44 of the 56 next-line
  directives lack a ` -- ` reason). 43 of the 49 hide live findings under the
  root config: for example
  apps/integrated-math-2/components/student/TriangleOrderingPractice.tsx:1
  (`/* eslint-disable next/no-img-element */`) hides
  `next(no-img-element)` at 125:8, and the four `lib/convex/server.ts` copies
  hide `typescript(no-explicit-any)` errors. The hidden findings include
  errors (no-explicit-any, no-html-link-for-pages, rules-of-hooks,
  react-hooks purity) and warnings (exhaustive-deps, no-unused-vars,
  no-img-element).
- This disproves the zero-findings claim of the S2 Implement task:
  "No finding: every oxlint log has empty output with exit 0, so no
  behavior-preserving fix was needed" (plan.md:309). The logs are empty
  because 43 files suppress their findings, not because the code is clean.
  The paired control holds: all 27 workspace lint scripts exit 0
  (gates/s2/lint.exit, 27 lines of code 0).
- The committed guard adv 7 (scripts/__tests__/oxc-toolchain-gates.test.ts,
  line 1210) fails on the 43-file list and stays failing until Green resolves
  F1.

Nonblocking finding F2 (Nit):
- Strategy section 8, risk "Oxlint reads no file", cites a defense "Each lint
  log has a labeled count `on <n> files`. Parse `<n>`. It is above 0."
  (test-strategy.md:540). No S2 case parses a file count, and oxlint 1.93.0
  prints no per-run file count: a clean run prints nothing (verified:
  `npx oxlint --config .oxlintrc.json --max-warnings 0 <clean file>` gives
  empty output, exit 0). The defense as written cannot exist. The real
  defense is the case 4 probe plus the exact-form lint scripts. Default
  disposition: no change; record the row as superseded by case 4 at the next
  strategy revision.

